<title>INDIA: Indian 5-year bond cut-off set at 12.69 pct - RBI.</title>
<headline>Indian 5-year bond cut-off set at 12.69 pct - RBI.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Friday it set a cut-off of 12.69 percent at its 30 billion rupee auction of five-year federal government bonds.  </p>
<p>The RBI said it received 187 bids for 37.67 billion rupees of which it accepted 98 for 20.13 billion.</p>
<p>It said devolvement on the central bank was 8.84 billion rupees and on primary dealers 1.03 billion.</p>
<p>The weighted-average cut-off yield was 12.61 percent, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
